  "settings": {
    "description": "SS11.12 - the holdout validation of the alpha-mode changes, run after every tune decision was settled, and run again once the mislabelled incumbent below was fixed. That holdout run can no longer be repeated: the alpha holdout split is retired (#83) because one of its eight images, cutout-wordmark-aflac, was deleted from Wikimedia Commons, so --split holdout refuses to run and SS11.12's holdout column is unreproducible. Only --split tune runs, and it is the reproducible evidence for these arms, with SS11.3 (-17.10% for the tier-0 candidate). The incumbent is the alpha layout as shipped at the start of SS11, so the delta is what stabilizing v0.7 moves alpha mode by. The tier-0 candidate is A28@3 L22@4 C3@3 and the compact-tier candidate A16@3 L12@4 C1@3; both were chosen on tune by protecting the mostly-opaque subgroup rather than by taking the deltaE00-optimal corner. Every arm pins alpha_ac_count and alpha_ac_bits explicitly. They are applied on top of Tunables::DEFAULT, so an arm that omitted them inherited the ADOPTED A28@3 -- which is what the incumbent labelled `SHIPPED A5@4` was doing: it encoded to 40 bytes rather than 32 and reported the adopted allocation's own alpha MAE, so this sweep was scoring the adopted layout against itself with a different luma/chroma split. Same defect class as EXPERIMENTS.md 9.5's seven configs; this one was not among them.",
